WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.650
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.990
- [Narrator] Perhaps the
only thing more anticipated

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.720
on Super Bowl Sunday than the game itself.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.077
- Puppy Monkey Baby.
- He's got Smaht Pahk.

00:00:09.077 --> 00:00:10.200
- I'm on a horse.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.640
- [Narrator] Are the commercials.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.530
- You can't just wear my face.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:15.990
- [Narrator] And many of
the most iconic commercials

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.760
are beer ads from the funny.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.950
- How you doing.
- How you doing.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.133
- Whassup?
- Whassup?

00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:22.966
- Whassup?

00:00:22.966 --> 00:00:24.257
- [Narrator] To the poignant.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:27.630
(pensive music)

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.130
But for 33 years,

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.512
these beer ads have had
one thing in common.

00:00:31.512 --> 00:00:34.470
♪ When you say Bud, you've said it all ♪

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.410
- [Narrator] Anheuser-Busch
InBev has been the only company

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.140
permitted to advertise
alcohol during the Super Bowl,

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.960
thanks to an exclusivity
deal with the NFL.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.600
Budweiser took full
advantage of that agreement.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.100
And for the past two decades,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.320
the brewer outspent all other brands

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.480
in advertising at the Super Bowl.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.330
But this year, Budweiser
is calling an audible

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.550
and giving up its grip on the event.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.500
And that has opened the door to beer

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.930
and alcohol companies that
have long been excluded

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.130
from the big game.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.440
- Anheuser-Busch giving
up their exclusivity

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.633
on that game is a huge deal.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.520
(pensive music)

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.620
- [Narrator] Super Bowls
are consistently ranked

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:14.430
as the most watched annual
television broadcast in America.

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:16.680
Although ratings have
declined in recent years,

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.570
last year, the big game attracted
over 112 million viewers.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.790
According to the analytics firm Kantar,

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:27.000
there are approximately
80 to 100 ads aired

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.440
during each Super Bowl.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.660
That works out to a total advertising time

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:34.680
of about 50 minutes or
roughly 30 seconds per ad.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.800
Purchasing a commercial during
the big game isn't cheap.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.710
In 2022, each 30-second ad slot went

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.590
for as much as $6.5 million.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:44.690
- I got some bad news.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.280
- [Narrator] So after previously paying

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.220
for the privilege to keep its
competitors off the field,

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:52.350
why is Budweiser changing course?

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.020
- Now, how is that supposed to sell beer?

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:58.320
- Even though Anheuser-Busch
gave up their exclusive right

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.090
to be the only alcohol advertiser

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:01.590
in the Super Bowl doesn't mean

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.480
that Super Bowl is not impactful

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.160
from a business point of view.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:07.500
Anheuser-Busch is still
spending tons of money

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.470
during the game on ads, and
what they've said publicly

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:12.240
is that they're basically gonna use some

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.270
of the money that they used
on that for other things.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:17.010
So when you think about Super Bowl,

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:18.450
it happens in the middle of February.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.270
It's not really the prime
selling season for beer.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:22.260
That happens in summer.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.670
So you could imagine that a company

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.800
like AB might save some of that money

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.590
and spend it when you know
sales are really high.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.930
- [Narrator] Although
Anheuser-Busch InBev has effectively

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:34.290
had a monopoly on Super
Bowl beer ads since 1989,

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:36.270
other brands have found creative ways

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.430
into the conversation
surrounding the game,

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:41.550
such as buying ad time in local
markets around the country.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:45.240
- Beer brands have really had
to bend over backwards to try

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.000
and steal the buzz, and
they've for years depended

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.980
on these gorilla marketing campaigns

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:53.040
to stimulate Super Bowl buzz
without actually buying ads.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.480
And it's a fraction of the price

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.490
and you're still getting press

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:59.580
and you're also seen
in really big markets.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:00.480
- [Announcer] This is a stunt designed

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.220
to make you miss our competitors.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:05.070
- One of the really successful
gorilla marketing campaigns

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:07.500
that a rival brewer had
run a couple years ago

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.390
was won by Miller Lite.

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.330
They basically ran a contest
where they offered free beer

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:15.450
for consumers, basically
saying when they see

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.490
the Michelob Ultra, ad to go

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:20.610
to the web and type in
this extra long URL.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:22.380
So basically that's stealing the traffic

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.520
that other people would've been searching

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:25.650
for that brand and it got 'em a lot

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:27.030
of publicity leading up to the game,

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:28.500
even though they didn't
have a Super Bowl ad

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:29.940
in the game itself.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:31.560
- [Narrator] For this year's Super Bowl,

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.840
viewers can expect to see spirit brands,

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.120
like Remy Martin and Crown Royal Whiskey.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.310
- Peanut butter? What?

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.570
- [Narrator] Crown Royal is seizing

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.670
on the opportunity to compete.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:44.220
Dave Grohl of Foo Fighters
is already being featured

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.540
in a teaser designed

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.240
to elicit interest in
the big game's ad spot.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.560
- The egg carton?

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.150
- So I think the biggest beneficiary

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:54.510
of Anheuser-Busch's change
will be Molson Coors.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:57.330
The company actually is really creative

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.490
because they've learned to sort of try

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:01.380
and find their way to steal the buzz

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:03.870
and this year they've used
that creativity to come

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.493
up with this huge program.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:08.490
- [Narrator] After an over 30-year hiatus,

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:11.670
Molson Coors recently
ran ads asking consumers

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:13.620
which of its two lite beers, Miller Lite

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:17.310
or Coors Lite deserves the
brewer's coveted Super Bowl spot.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.720
- They've teamed up with DraftKings,

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.450
which is really smart given how everybody

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:22.950
in this nation is obsessed

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.810
with sports online betting right now.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:28.680
So what consumers can do is
go and figure out like, oh,

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.470
I think this is what they're...

00:04:31.446 --> 00:04:32.279
Will it be Miller?

00:04:32.279 --> 00:04:33.144
Will it be Coors?

00:04:33.144 --> 00:04:34.830
(playful music)

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:35.663
- Oh, hey.

00:04:35.663 --> 00:04:37.320
- [Narrator] Heineken will
also make an appearance

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:38.153
this year. 

00:04:38.153 --> 00:04:40.020
The Dutch brand is teaming up with Marvel

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.360
to promote the upcoming "Ant-Man" film

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.963
and its alcohol-free brew Heineken 0.0.

00:04:45.963 --> 00:04:48.030
(clanging sound)
(can opening)

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:51.720
Despite giving up its exclusivity
agreement with the NFL,

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.240
Anheuser-Busch InBev brands like Bud Light

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:55.740
and Michelob Ultra will still

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:58.740
have a presence in the
game on February 12th.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:00.240
- [Announcer] Who drinks Budweiser.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.680
- [Narrator] But on the national stage,

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.423
Budweiser won't be appearing.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:06.300
- [Announcer] They say
all people are six degrees

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.370
of separation away from each other.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:09.630
- [Narrator] In regional markets,

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:11.670
Budweiser will run an ad that features

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:14.580
a Kevin Bacon voiceover
with a nod to the concept

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:19.080
of six degrees of separation,
all facilitated by a six pack.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.990
- [Announcer] People who
share the same spirit

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:23.223
share the same beer.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:26.763
This Bud's for you.

